@startuml overview
' cumin-works - the states of a requirement issue in the plan.
' A state is a label on GitHub, written without "cumin/status/". "do /" says who works in the state.
' A transition is written: action [guard] / what cumin does.
' Render: run scripts/render-diagrams.sh at the root of the repository.

hide empty description

state "Draft (no status label)" as Draft
Draft : do / a Maintainer writes the requirement

state "ready" as Ready
Ready : do / cumin waits for a free slot

state "planning" as Planning
Planning : do / the Planner plans

state "awaiting-plan-review" as PlanReview
PlanReview : do / the Assignee reviews the plan

state "implementing" as Implementing
Implementing : do / the agents work on the sub-issues

state "awaiting-decision" as Decision
Decision : do / the Assignee answers

state "accepting" as Accepting #EEEEEE
Accepting : (the acceptance area)

[*] --> Draft
Draft --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready
Ready --> Planning : request the split\n[cumin handles the ready, the blockers are closed,\ncumin has a free slot]\n/ cumin starts the Planner
Planning --> PlanReview : ask for the plan review\n[no Planner runs, the plan is complete,\na sub-issue is open]\n/ cumin notifies
Planning --> Planning : request the split again\n[no Planner runs, the plan is not complete,\nno question, first time]\n/ cumin starts the Planner again
Planning --> Decision : stop the split\n[no Planner runs, and: the Planner asked,\nor the plan is not complete after the retry]\n/ cumin notifies
Planning --> Accepting : [every sub-issue is closed]
PlanReview --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\n[the Assignee adds ready to a sub-issue]\n/ cumin changes the label
Draft --> Implementing : mark the requirement as in work\n[the Assignee adds ready to a sub-issue]
Implementing --> PlanReview : ask about the remaining sub-issues\n[only sub-issues without a status label remain]\n/ cumin notifies
Decision --> Ready : a Maintainer adds ready

@enduml
